    "content": "commit 92ee10d5ba0fe89a9b48ce0be3a7f7f55c00d363\nAuthor: Martin von Gagern <gagern@google.com>\nDate:   Tue Jun 30 11:54:35 2020 +0100\n\n    Restore attribute handling with empty block_id\n\n    Commit 08c3e4f48b2cf137f1848e789d6b5d21075b4e65 had been aiming to be a\n    semantic no-op in its attribute handling. But I had missed the fact that\n    with empty block_id any characters between '@' and ' ' would cause the match\n    to fail. This can be important e.g. when there are JavaDoc comments in code\n    as these are likely to start with \"{@\".\n\n    The sequence \"{@ \" can be used to introduce an extended comment inside a\n    code block. I'm not sure whether that's a bug or a feature, so I'm\n    documenting it in the test case for now, so that any change in behavior\n    there will at least be deliberate.\n---\n src/document.c                                     |  9 ++++-----\n test/Tests/extras/Special_Attribute_CodeBlock.html | 19 +++++++++++++++++++\n test/Tests/extras/Special_Attribute_CodeBlock.text | 17 +++++++++++++++++\n test/config.json                                   |  5 +++++\n 4 files changed, 45 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)\n\ndiff --git a/src/document.c b/src/document.c\nindex ca9fc07..79b24e1 100644\n--- a/src/document.c\n+++ b/src/document.c\n@@ -697,13 +697,12 @@ static size_t parse_attributes(uint8_t *data, size_t size, struct hoedown_buffer\n                                }\n                                /* it might have matched only the first portion of block_id; make sure\n                                 * there's no more to it here */\n-                               if (*block_id || (begin < end && data[begin] != ' ')) {\n+                               if (*block_id) {\n                                        return len;\n                                }\n-                       } else {\n-                               while (begin < end && data[begin] != ' ') {\n-                                       begin++;\n-                               }\n+                       }\n+                       if (begin < end && data[begin] != ' ') {\n+                               return len;\n                        }\n                        if (block_attr) {\n                                if (block_attr->size) {\ndiff --git a/test/Tests/extras/Special_Attribute_CodeBlock.html b/test/Tests/extras/Special_Attribute_CodeBlock.html\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..25566e9\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/test/Tests/extras/Special_Attribute_CodeBlock.html\n@@ -0,0 +1,19 @@\n+<p>This is a space-indented code block.</p>\n+\n+<pre><code>{\n+  /** JavaDoc with a {@link #somewhere}\n+   */\n+}\n+</code></pre>\n+\n+<p>The link is <em>not</em> an extended attribute!</p>\n+\n+<pre><code class=\"codesample\">{\n+  /** Code with attribute\n+   */\n+}\n+</code></pre>\n+\n+<p>The above <em>is</em> an extended attribute, at least for now.\n+See <a href=\"https://github.com/kjdev/hoextdown/issues/62\">#62</a> for a discussion about\n+whether this kind of syntax should be supported.</p>\ndiff --git a/test/Tests/extras/Special_Attribute_CodeBlock.text b/test/Tests/extras/Special_Attribute_CodeBlock.text\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..23cfde6\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/test/Tests/extras/Special_Attribute_CodeBlock.text\n@@ -0,0 +1,17 @@\n+This is a space-indented code block.\n+\n+    {\n+      /** JavaDoc with a {@link #somewhere}\n+       */\n+    }\n+\n+The link is *not* an extended attribute!\n+\n+    {\n+      /** Code with attribute\n+       */\n+    } {@ .codesample }\n+\n+The above *is* an extended attribute, at least for now.\n+See [#62](https://github.com/kjdev/hoextdown/issues/62) for a discussion about\n+whether this kind of syntax should be supported.\ndiff --git a/test/config.json b/test/config.json\nindex 5643817..28e3acd 100644\n--- a/test/config.json\n+++ b/test/config.json\n@@ -166,6 +166,11 @@\n             \"output\": \"Tests/extras/Special_Attribute_FencedCode.html\",\n             \"flags\": [\"--special-attribute\", \"--fenced-code\"]\n         },\n+        {\n+            \"input\": \"Tests/extras/Special_Attribute_CodeBlock.text\",\n+            \"output\": \"Tests/extras/Special_Attribute_CodeBlock.html\",\n+            \"flags\": [\"--special-attribute\"]\n+        },\n         {\n             \"input\": \"Tests/extras/Special_Attribute_Codespan.text\",\n             \"output\": \"Tests/extras/Special_Attribute_Codespan.html\",",
